<h2>Questions from Jamestown property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>My older Jamestown home has plaster walls and original trim. Does that affect a water damage claim?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Repairing plaster and matching original millwork costs more than standard drywall and stock trim. If an estimate prices your home as if it were new construction, that gap is worth reviewing.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you handle hail claims on farm buildings outside Jamestown?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Barns, machine sheds and shops are often underscoped. We review the policy limits for those structures and price the repairs accurately.</p></div></details><details><summary>Will my homeowners policy cover water from the James River rising in spring?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Generally not. Standard homeowners policies exclude flood, including river overflow. That kind of loss is typically handled under a separate NFIP or private flood policy.</p></div></details></div>
